    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="A Trapezoid Surprise" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="57.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="ABDC is a trapezoid with bases AB and CD. E and H are the midpoints of the bases.\n\nDraw the diagonals and the lines from the midpoints, as shown. Lines through the crossing points cut the base AB into three equal parts: AL = LM = MB.\n\nDrag the vertices — it always works." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="105.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
